EADME.md: (404) Not Found\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nGet Started with the Azure MCP Server - Azure MCP Server | Microsoft Learn (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/developer/azure-mcp-server/get-started)\\\\nciteturn2view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\\\\\\\"ref_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/developer/azure-mcp-server/get-started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"lineno\\\\\\\":null}); Total lines: 128\\\\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content cite1†Skip to Ask Learn chat experience L1: \\\\nL2: This browser is no longer supported.\\\\nL3: \\\\nL4: Upgrade to Microsoft Edge to take advantage of the latest features, security updates, and technical support.\\\\nL5: \\\\nL6: cite2†Download Microsoft Edge†go.microsoft.com cite3†More info about Internet Explorer and Microsoft Edge L7: \\\\nL8: Table of contents Exit editor mode\\\\nL9: \\\\nL10: Ask Learn Ask Learn\\\\nL11: \\\\nL12: Reading mode Table of contents cite1†Read in English Add Add to Plans cite4†Edit†github.com L13: \\\\nL14: * * *\\\\nL15: \\\\nL16: Copy Markdown Print\\\\nL17: \\\\nL18: * * *\\\\nL19: \\\\nL20: Note\\\\nL21: Access to this page requires authorization. You can try cite1†signing in or changing directories.\\\\nL22: \\\\nL23: Access to this page requires authorization. You can try changing directories.\\\\nL24: # Get started with the Azure MCP Server\\\\nL25: \\\\nL26: Feedback\\\\nL27: \\\\nL28: Summarize this article for me\\\\nL29: ## In this article\\\\nL30: \\\\nL31: The cite5†Azure MCP Server enables AI-powered development tools to interact with Azure cloud services through the Model Context Protocol (MCP). It provides a unified way to manage Azure resources, deploy applications, and query cloud services directly from your development environment.\\\\nL32: Connect to Azure MCP Server using various tools, languages, and frameworks. Use it to manage Azure resources through natural language conversations, build automation scripts, or integrate Azure operations into your applications.\\\\nL33: \\\\nL34: Explore and contribute to the cite6†Azure MCP Server on GitHub†github.com .\\\\nL35: ## Install Azure MCP Server using a package manager\\\\nL36: \\\\nL37: You can optionally install Azure MCP Server directly using one of the supported package managers. Package manager installation offers several advantages, including centralized dependency management, CI/CD integration, support for headless environments, version control, and project portability.\\\\nL38: \\\\nL39: Note\\\\nL40: You don't need to install the Azure MCP Server to use it. The approaches explained in the cite7†Connect to Azure MCP Server section either include Azure MCP Server as part of their installation, or run Azure MCP Server directly via package manager commands.\\\\nL41: \\\\nL42: For more information, see cite8†Install with a package manager†github.com .\\\\nL43: \\\\nL44:   * NuGet: cite9†Azure.Mcp†www.nuget.org L45:   * NPM: cite10†@azure/mcp†www.npmjs.com L46:   * PyPI: cite11†msmcp-azure†pypi.org L47: ## Connect to Azure MCP Server\\\\nL48: \\\\nL49: You can connect to Azure MCP Server using the following tools and programming frameworks.\\\\nL50: \\\\nL51: ### Use a code editor\\\\nL52: \\\\nL53: Azure MCP Server works with AI-powered code editors and tools that support the Model Context Protocol. Learn how to get started:\\\\nL54: \\\\nL55:   * cite12†Cline L56:   * cite13†Cursor L57:   * cite14†Google Antigravity L58:   * cite15†IntelliJ L59:   * cite16†Visual Studio L60:   * cite17†Visual Studio Code L61:   * cite18†Windsurf L62: ### Use GitHub Copilot tools\\\\nL63: \\\\nL64: Connect to Azure MCP Server using other tools and services, such as GitHub Copilot cloud agent and Docker. Learn how to get started:\\\\nL65: \\\\nL66:   * cite19†GitHub Copilot CLI L67:   * cite20†GitHub Copilot SDK L68:   * cite21†GitHub Copilot cloud agent L69: \\\\nL70: ### Use a Docker container\\\\nL71: \\\\nL72: For easy deployment and isolation, you can cite22†run the Azure MCP server as a Docker container†github.com .\\\\nL73: ### Use programming languages & frameworks\\\\nL74: \\\\nL75: Connect to Azure MCP Server using programming languages and frameworks. This documentation currently provides guidance and examples for Python and .NET.\\\\nL76: #### Python\\\\nL77: \\\\nL78: cite23†Get started with Azure MCP Server and Python to enhance your apps and workflows.\\\\nL79: \\\\nL80:   * Use Python MCP client libraries to connect directly to Azure MCP Server.\\\\nL81:   * Build automation scripts that manage Azure resources.\\\\nL82:   * Integrate into web frameworks like Django, Flask, or FastAPI.\\\\nL83:   * Incorporate Azure operations into data science workflows with Jupyter notebooks.\\\\nL84: #### .NET\\\\nL85: \\\\nL86: cite24†Get started with Azure MCP Server and .NET to enhance your apps and workflows.\\\\nL87: \\\\nL88:   * Create console applications and command-line tools for Azure management.\\\\nL89:   * Build ASP.NET Core web applications with integrated Azure capabilities.\\\\nL90:   * Develop Azure Functions that leverage Azure MCP Server for resource management.\\\\nL91:   * Create Windows desktop applications with Azure integration.\\\\nL92: The Azure MCP Server provides flexibility to work with Azure in the way that best fits your development style and requirements, whether through interactive AI-powered editors or programmatic integration in your applications.\\\\nL93: \\\\nL94: * * *\\\\nL95: ## Feedback\\\\nL96: \\\\nL97: Was this page helpful?\\\\nL98: \\\\nL99: Yes No No\\\\nL100: \\\\nL101: Need help with this topic?\\\\nL102: \\\\nL103: Want to try using Ask Learn to clarify or guide you through this topic?\\\\nL104: \\\\nL105: Ask Learn Ask Learn\\\\nL106: \\\\nL107: Suggest a fix?\\\\nL108: \\\\nL109: * * *\\\\nL110: \\\\nL111: ## Additional resources\\\\nL112: \\\\nL113: * * *\\\\nL114: \\\\nL115:   * Last updated on 2026-06-29\\\\nL116: \\\\nL117: ### In this article\\\\nL118: \\\\nL119: Was this page helpful?\\\\nL120: \\\\nL121: Need help with this topic?\\\\nL122: \\\\nL123: Want to try using Ask Learn to clarify or guide you through this topic?\\\\nL124: \\\\nL125: Ask Learn Ask Learn\\\\nL126: \\\\nL127: Suggest a fix?\\\\n\\\",\\\"search_results\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text_result\\\",\\\"ref_id\\\":\\\"turn2view0\\\",\\\"snippet\\\":\\\"Total lines: 1\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Internal Error\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text_result\\\",\\\"domain\\\":\\\"learn.microsoft.com\\\",\\\"ref_id\\\":\\\"turn2view1\\\",\\\"snippet\\\":\\\"Total lines: 128\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Get Started with the Azure MCP Server - Azure MCP Server | Microsoft Learn\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/developer/azure-mcp-server/get-started\\\"}]}\"}]"},"sessionId":"2026-09-23T03-58-32-231Z_01a0cc6a-4726-71f4-b47c-57674e2cf3d3","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:02:09.691Z","toolInput":"{\"code\":\"const r=await tools.web__run({open:[{ref_id:\\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/mcp/main/servers/Azure.Mcp/README.md\\\"},{ref_id:\\\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/developer/azure-mcp-server/get-started\\\"}],response_length:\\\"long\\\"}); text(r)\\n\"}","toolName":"exec","toolOutput":"[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\\"output_text\\\":\\\"Internal Error ()\\\\nciteturn2view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\\\\\\\"ref_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/mcp/main/servers/Azure.Mcp/README.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"lineno\\\\\\\":null}); Total lines: 1\\\\nL0: Failed to fetch https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/mcp/main/servers/Azure.Mcp/README.md: (404) Not Found\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nGet Started with the Azure MCP Server - Azure MCP Server | Microsoft Learn (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/a