 ### Use programming languages & frameworks\\\\nL74: \\\\nL75: Connect to Azure MCP Server using programming languages and frameworks. This documentation currently provides guidance and examples for Python and .NET.\\\\nL76: #### Python\\\\nL77: \\\\nL78: cite23†Get started with Azure MCP Server and Python to enhance your apps and workflows.\\\\nL79: \\\\nL80:   * Use Python MCP client libraries to connect directly to Azure MCP Server.\\\\nL81:   * Build automation scripts that manage Azure resources.\\\\nL82:   * Integrate into web frameworks like Django, Flask, or FastAPI.\\\\nL83:   * Incorporate Azure operations into data science workflows with Jupyter notebooks.\\\\nL84: #### .NET\\\\nL85: \\\\nL86: cite24†Get started with Azure MCP Server and .NET to enhance your apps and workflows.\\\\nL87: \\\\nL88:   * Create console applications and command-line tools for Azure management.\\\\nL89:   * Build ASP.NET Core web applications with integrated Azure capabilities.\\\\nL90:   * Develop Azure Functions that leverage Azure MCP Server for resource management.\\\\nL91:   * Create Windows desktop applications with Azure integration.\\\\nL92: The Azure MCP Server provides flexibility to work with Azure in the way that best fits your development style and requirements, whether through interactive AI-powered editors or programmatic integration in your applications.\\\\nL93: \\\\nL94: * * *\\\\nL95: ## Feedback\\\\nL96: \\\\nL97: Was this page helpful?\\\\nL98: \\\\nL99: Yes No No\\\\nL100: \\\\nL101: Need help with this topic?\\\\nL102: \\\\nL103: Want to try using Ask Learn to clarify or guide you through this topic?\\\\nL104: \\\\nL105: Ask Learn Ask Learn\\\\nL106: \\\\nL107: Suggest a fix?\\\\nL108: \\\\nL109: * * *\\\\nL110: \\\\nL111: ## Additional resources\\\\nL112: \\\\nL113: * * *\\\\nL114: \\\\nL115:   * Last updated on 2026-06-29\\\\nL116: \\\\nL117: ### In this article\\\\nL118: \\\\nL119: Was this page helpful?\\\\nL120: \\\\nL121: Need help with this topic?\\\\nL122: \\\\nL123: Want to try using Ask Learn to clarify or guide you through this topic?\\\\nL124: \\\\nL125: Ask Learn Ask Learn\\\\nL126: \\\\nL127: Suggest a fix?\\\\n\\\",\\\"search_results\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text_result\\\",\\\"ref_id\\\":\\\"turn2view0\\\",\\\"snippet\\\":\\\"Total lines: 1\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Internal Error\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text_result\\\",\\\"domain\\\":\\\"learn.microsoft.com\\\",\\\"ref_id\\\":\\\"turn2view1\\\",\\\"snippet\\\":\\\"Total lines: 128\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Get Started with the Azure MCP Server - Azure MCP Server | Microsoft Learn\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/developer/azure-mcp-server/get-started\\\"}]}\"}]"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mudku81k_1585636f28c5":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mudku81k_1585636f28c5","origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-23T04:02:22.853Z","channel":"tool","detail":"exec"},"raw":{"tool_input":"{\"code\":\"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\\\"git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/microsoft/mcp.git /tmp/microsoft-mcp >/dev/null 2>&1 && find /tmp/microsoft-mcp -maxdepth 4 -iname '*readme*' | grep -i azure | head; rg -n 'app.?registration|virtual network|vm|admin|azure mcp|npx @azure/mcp' /tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers -g 'README*' -g '*.md' | head -80\\\",workdir:\\\"/home/chris/01_Projects/azure/homelab\\\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:4000}); text(r.output)\\n\"}","tool_name":"exec","tool_output":"[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/azd-templates/README.md\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/README.md\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Fabric.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:25:- Renamed the `docs` toolset's `--workload-type` parameter to `--item-type`, aligning it with `core_create-item`'s existing `--item-type` and with official Fabric terminology. The accepted values are almost all Fabric item types (`notebook`, `lakehouse`, `dataPipeline`, `report`, ...); the description now also enumerates the four non-item API areas (`platform`, `admin`, `spark`, `realTimeIntelligence`). [[#3327](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/3327)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Fabric.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:219:- Added Admin APIs usage guidelines to help LLMs understand when to use admin APIs, request explicit user permission, and implement graceful fallbacks to standard APIs\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Fabric.Mcp.Server/README.md:240:| `docs_list-item-types` | Lists the Fabric item types that have public API specifications available, plus the non-item API areas (platform, admin, spark, realTimeIntelligence). |\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:40:    - [Working with Administrators](#working-with-administrators)\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:352:If you encounter this error in an enterprise environment, work with your resource administrator to:\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:359:2. **Confirm Authentication Method**: Ask your administrator:\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:663:   Ask your Azure administrator to create a service principal with this information:\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:816:**To your resource administrator:**\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:828:**To your network administrator:**\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:843:**To your identity administrator:**\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:856:| 1 | Resource administrator | RBAC role assignments, resource-specific permissions |\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:857:| 2 | Network administrator | Firewall rules, private endpoints, proxy configuration |\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:858:| 3 | Identity administrator | Conditional Access policies, service principal creation |\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:862:**Resource administrator:**\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:867:**Network administrator:**\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:873:**Identity administrator:**\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:893:- Contact your organization's IT administrator to gain access to your company's Azure subscription\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:1149:   az ad app permission admin-consent --id <client-id>\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:1167:   az ad app permission admin-consent --id <server-client-id>\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/azd-templates/api-permissions.md:28:You can add the desirable API Permissions to your app registration using Azure CLI. Learn more at [az ad app permission add](https://learn.microsoft.com/cli/azure/ad/app/permission?view=azure-cli-latest#az-ad-app-permission-add)\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:475:- Added support for AVM pattern modules (`avm-ptn-*`) in the Azure Terraform `avm` tools. The `azureterraform avm list` tool now returns both resource and pattern modules, each tagged with a `moduleType` field, and `avm versions`/`avm get` work for pattern modules as well as resource modules. [[#2946](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2946)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:624:- The `compute vm delete` and `compute vmss delete` tools now return a not-found outcome (`Success: false`) when the target resource does not exist, instead of reporting a successful deletion. This may affect automation that previously treated non-existent VM/VMSS deletions as success. [[#2687](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2687)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:636:    - `vm update` and `vmss update` now correctly clear all tags when `--tags ''` is passed.\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:651:- Added more validations to the `compute vm create` and `compute vmss create` tools. [[#2764](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2764)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:680:  - `keyvault admin settings get` now correctly applies the default retry policy\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:695:- Added a tool for managing VM power state (start/stop/restart/deallocate) called `compute_vm_power-state`. [[#2498](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2498)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:747:- Added `Ubuntu2604` image alias for `azmcp vm create` mapping to marketplace URN `Canonical:ubuntu-26_04-lts:server:latest`. [[#2533](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2533)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:751:- Updated `azmcp compute vm create` and `azmcp compute vmss create` to require the `--image` parameter, removing the default `Ubuntu 24.04 LTS` image when omitted. Users must now specify an alias, Marketplace URN, or shared gallery image ID. [[#2533](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2533)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:754:- Removed the `Ubuntu2004` image alias from `azmcp vm create`. `Ubuntu 20.04` LTS reached end of standard support on May 31, 2025 and is no longer recommended for new VMs. Use `Ubuntu2204` or `Ubuntu2404`, or specify the Marketplace URN (`Canonical:0001-com-ubuntu-server-focal:20_04-lts-gen2:latest`) if `Ubuntu 20.04` is still required. [[#2533](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2533)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:803:  - `azureterraform_avm_list`\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:804:  - `azureterraform_avm_versions`\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:805:  - `azureterraform_avm_get`\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:822:- Fixed RSV IaaS VM protection in `azurebackup protecteditem protect` by submitting the protect request directly (removing the 180s container-discovery pre-poll), preventing timeouts for newly created VMs and matching `az backup protection enable-for-vm` behavior. [[#2470](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2470)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:858:- Changed default VM size for `vm create` and `vmss create` commands from `Standard_DS1_v2` (older generation) to `Standard_D2s_v5` (2 vCPU, 8 GB RAM, D-series v5) [[#2415](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2415)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:879:- Fixed `compute_vmss_update` tool returning HTTP 400 when only `--capacity`, `--overprovision`, or `--enable-auto-os-upgrade` is provided by correcting option type definitions to use nullable types. [[#2421](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2421)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:962:- **npm**: Run `npx @azure/mcp@2.0.0`\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:1216:  - `compute_vm_delete`\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:1217:  - `compute_vmss_delete`\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:1650:- Added Azure Compute VM operations with flexible compute vm get command that supports listing all VMs in a subscription, listing VMs in a resource group, getting specific VM details, and retrieving VM instance view with runtime status: [[#1482](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/1482)]\\n/"},"sessionId":"2026-09-23T03-58-32-231Z_01a0cc6a-4726-71f4-b47c-57674e2cf3d3","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:02:22.853Z","toolInput":"{\"code\":\"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\\\"git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/microsoft/mcp.git /tmp/microsoft-mcp >/dev/null 2>&1 && find /tmp/microsoft-mcp -maxdepth 4 -iname '*readme*' | grep -i azure | head; rg -n 'app.?registration|virtual network|vm|admin|azure mcp|npx @azure/mcp' /tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers -g 'README*' -g '*.md' | head -80\\\",workdir:\\\"/home/chris/01_Projects/azure/homelab\\\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:4000}); text(r.output)\\n\"}","toolName":"exec","toolOutput":"[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/azd-templates/README.md\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/README.md\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Fabric.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:25:- Renamed the `docs` toolset's `--workload-type` parameter to `--item-type`, aligning it with `core_create-item`'s existing `--item-type` and with official Fabric terminology. The accepted values are almost all Fabric item types (`notebook`, `lakehouse`, `dataPipeline`, `report`, ...); the description now also enumerates the four non-item API areas (`platform`, `admin`, `spark`, `realTimeIntelligence`). [[#3327](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/3327)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Fabric.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:219:- Added Admin APIs usage guidelines to help LLMs understand when to use admin APIs, request explicit user permission, and implement graceful fallbacks to standard APIs\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Fabric.Mcp.Server/README.md:240:| `docs_list-item-types` | Lists the Fabric item types that have public API specifications available, plus the non-item API areas (platform, admin, spark, realTimeIntelligence). |\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:40:    - [Working with Administrators](#working-with-administrators)\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:352:If you encounter this error in an enterprise environment, work with your resource administrator to:\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:359:2. **Confirm Authentication Method**: Ask your administrator:\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:663:   Ask your Azure administrator to create a service principal with this information:\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:816:**To your resource administrator