/`avm get` work for pattern modules as well as resource modules. [[#2946](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2946)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:624:- The `compute vm delete` and `compute vmss delete` tools now return a not-found outcome (`Success: false`) when the target resource does not exist, instead of reporting a successful deletion. This may affect automation that previously treated non-existent VM/VMSS deletions as success. [[#2687](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2687)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:636:    - `vm update` and `vmss update` now correctly clear all tags when `--tags ''` is passed.\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:651:- Added more validations to the `compute vm create` and `compute vmss create` tools. [[#2764](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2764)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:680:  - `keyvault admin settings get` now correctly applies the default retry policy\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:695:- Added a tool for managing VM power state (start/stop/restart/deallocate) called `compute_vm_power-state`. [[#2498](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2498)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:747:- Added `Ubuntu2604` image alias for `azmcp vm create` mapping to marketplace URN `Canonical:ubuntu-26_04-lts:server:latest`. [[#2533](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2533)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:751:- Updated `azmcp compute vm create` and `azmcp compute vmss create` to require the `--image` parameter, removing the default `Ubuntu 24.04 LTS` image when omitted. Users must now specify an alias, Marketplace URN, or shared gallery image ID. [[#2533](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2533)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:754:- Removed the `Ubuntu2004` image alias from `azmcp vm create`. `Ubuntu 20.04` LTS reached end of standard support on May 31, 2025 and is no longer recommended for new VMs. Use `Ubuntu2204` or `Ubuntu2404`, or specify the Marketplace URN (`Canonical:0001-com-ubuntu-server-focal:20_04-lts-gen2:latest`) if `Ubuntu 20.04` is still required. [[#2533](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2533)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:803:  - `azureterraform_avm_list`\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:804:  - `azureterraform_avm_versions`\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:805:  - `azureterraform_avm_get`\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:822:- Fixed RSV IaaS VM protection in `azurebackup protecteditem protect` by submitting the protect request directly (removing the 180s container-discovery pre-poll), preventing timeouts for newly created VMs and matching `az backup protection enable-for-vm` behavior. [[#2470](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2470)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:858:- Changed default VM size for `vm create` and `vmss create` commands from `Standard_DS1_v2` (older generation) to `Standard_D2s_v5` (2 vCPU, 8 GB RAM, D-series v5) [[#2415](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2415)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:879:- Fixed `compute_vmss_update` tool returning HTTP 400 when only `--capacity`, `--overprovision`, or `--enable-auto-os-upgrade` is provided by correcting option type definitions to use nullable types. [[#2421](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/2421)]\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:962:- **npm**: Run `npx @azure/mcp@2.0.0`\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:1216:  - `compute_vm_delete`\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:1217:  - `compute_vmss_delete`\\n/tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/CHANGELOG.md:1650:- Added Azure Compute VM operations with flexible compute vm get command that supports listing all VMs in a subscription, listing VMs in a resource group, getting specific VM details, and retrieving VM instance view with runtime status: [[#1482](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/pull/1482)]\\n/"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mudkubjd_2babf3c039bf":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mudkubjd_2babf3c039bf","origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-23T04:02:27.346Z","channel":"tool","detail":"exec"},"raw":{"tool_input":"{\"code\":\"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\\\"rg -n 'MCP|mcpServers|npx|network|entra|app registration|app registration' /tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/README.md | head -60; sed -n '1,130p' /tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/README.md; rg -n 'app.*(create|list)|entra.*app|virtual network|vnet' /tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/README.md | head -40\\\",workdir:\\\"/home/chris/01_Projects/azure/homelab\\\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:4500}); text(r.output)\\n\"}","tool_name":"exec","tool_output":"[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"jetbrains.com/plugin/8053) [![Install Azure MCP in Eclipse](https://img.shields.io/badge/Eclipse-Install_Azure_MCP_Server-b6ae1d?style=flat-square&logo=eclipse&logoColor=white)](https://marketplace.eclipse.org/content/azure-toolkit-eclipse)\\n19:[![MCP Toplist](https://mcptoplist.com/badge/com.microsoft%2Fazure.svg)](https://mcptoplist.com/server/com.microsoft%2Fazure)\\n41:        - [MCPB](#mcpb)<!-- remove-section: end remove_installation_sub_sections -->\\n46:    - [What can you do with the Azure MCP Server?](#what-can-you-do-with-the-azure-mcp-server)\\n63:**Azure MCP Server** supercharges your agents with Azure context across numerous Azure services.\\n66:<!-- insert-section: vsix {{- Install the [Azure MCP Server Visual Studio Code extension](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=ms-azuretools.vscode-azure-mcp-server)}} -->\\n67:<!-- insert-section: vsix {{- Start (or Auto-Start) the MCP Server}} -->\\n68:<!-- insert-section: vsix {{   > **VS Code (version 1.103 or above):** You can now configure MCP servers to start automatically using the `chat.mcp.autostart` setting, instead of manually restarting them after configuration changes.}} -->\\n73:<!-- insert-section: vsix {{   3. Select **newAndOutdated** to automatically start MCP servers without manual refresh.}} -->\\n75:<!-- insert-section: vsix {{      ![VS Code MCP Autostart Tooltip](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/mcp/main/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/images/vsix/ToolTip.png)}}-->\\n79:<!-- insert-section: vsix {{   2. Run `MCP: List Servers`.}} -->\\n83:<!-- insert-section: vsix {{   3. Select `Azure MCP Server ext`, then click **Start Server**.}} -->\\n108:<!-- insert-section: vsix {{   - Changes take effect after restarting the Azure MCP server from the MCP: List Servers view. (Step 2)}} -->\\n110:<!-- insert-section: vsix {{You’re all set! Azure MCP Server is now ready to help you work smarter with Azure resources in VS Code.}} -->\\n113:Install Azure MCP Server using either an IDE extension or package manager. Choose one method below.\\n116:> Authenticate to Azure before running the Azure MCP server. See the [Authentication guide](https://github.com/microsoft/mcp/blob/main/docs/Authentication.md) for authentication methods and instructions.\\n120:Start using Azure MCP with your favorite IDE.  We recommend VS Code:\\n125:![Install Azure MCP Server Extension](images/install_azure_mcp_server_extension.gif)\\n128:1. Install the [Azure MCP Server](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=ms-azuretools.vscode-azure-mcp-server) extension.\\n162:1. In the editor's agent side panel, select **...** > **MCP Servers** > **Manage MCP Servers** > **View raw config**.\\n163:1. Add Azure MCP Server to the `mcpServers` object in `mcp_config.json`:\\n167:         \\\"mcpServers\\\": {\\n169:                 \\\"command\\\": \\\"npx\\\",\\n176:Antigravity stores global configuration at `~/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json`. For workspace-only configuration, use `.agents/mcp_config.json`. For more information, see the [Google Antigravity MCP documentation](https://antigravity.google/docs/mcp).\\n180:The Azure plugin packages the Azure MCP Server along with Azure-related agents and skills, bringing Azure integration to Claude Code in one installation.\\n191:Azure MCP Server can also be configured across other IDEs, CLIs, and MCP clients:\\n201:- To use Azure MCP server from .NET, you must have the latest [.NET 10 SDK LTS](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download/dotnet) installed. .NET 10 and later adds a command, dnx, which is used to download, install, and run the MCP server from [nuget.org](https://www.nuget.org).\\n207:        \\\"mcpServers\\\": {\\n228:#### Option 2: Configure using Node.js (npm/npx)<!-- remove-section: end remove_node_config_sub_header -->\\n229:- To use Azure MCP server from node one must have Node.js (LTS) installed and available on your system PATH — this provides both `npm` and `npx`. We recommend the latest Node.js LTS version. To verify your installation run: `node --version`, `npm --version`, and `npx --version`.\\n234:        \\\"mcpServers\\\": {\\n236:            \\\"command\\\": \\\"npx\\\",\\n251:- To use Azure MCP server from Python, you must have [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/) installed. uv is a fast Python package installer and resolver. To verify your installation run: `uv --version` and `uvx --version`.\\n256:        \\\"mcpServers\\\": {\\n272:**Note:** When manually configuring Visual Studio and Visual Studio Code, use `servers` instead of `mcpServers` as the root object.\\n277:| **VS Code** | `.vscode/mcp.json` (workspace)<br>`settings.json` (user) | [VS Code MCP Documentation](https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/copilot/chat/mcp-servers) |\\n278:| **Visual Studio** | `.mcp.json` (solution/workspace) | [Visual Studio MCP Setup](https://learn.microsoft.com/visualstudio/ide/mcp-servers?view=vs-2022) |\\n279:| **GitHub Copilot CLI** | `~/.copilot/mcp-config.json` | [Copilot CLI MCP Configuration](#github-copilot-cli-configuration) |\\n280:| **Claude Code** | `~/.claude.json` or `.mcp.json` (project) | [Claude Code MCP Configuration](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/mcp-quickstart#add-a-local-server) |\\n281:| **Eclipse IDE** | GitHub Copilot Chat -> Configure Tools -> MCP Servers  | [Eclipse MCP Documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/provide-context/use-mcp/extend-copilot-chat-with-mcp#configuring-mcp-servers-in-eclipse) |\\n282:| **IntelliJ IDEA** | Built-in MCP server (2025.2+)<br>Settings > Tools > MCP Server | [IntelliJ MCP Documentation](https://www.jetbrains.com/help/ai-assistant/mcp.html) |\\n283:| **Google Antigravity** | `~/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json` (global)<br>`.agents/mcp_config.json` (workspace) | [Google Antigravity MCP Documentation](https://antigravity.google/docs/mcp) |\\n284:| **Cursor** | `~/.cursor/mcp.json` or `.cursor/mcp.json` | [Cursor MCP Documentation](https://docs.cursor.com/context/model-context-protocol) |\\n285:| **Windsurf** | `~/.codeium/windsurf/mcp_config.json` | [Windsurf Cascade MCP Integration](https://docs.windsurf.com/windsurf/cascade/mcp) |\\n286:| **Amazon Q Developer** | `~/.aws/amazonq/mcp.json` (global)<br>`.amazonq/mcp.json` (workspace) | [AWS Q Developer MCP Guide](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonq/latest/qdeveloper-ug/qdev-mcp.html) |\\n287:| **Claude Desktop** | `~/.claude/claude_desktop_config.json` (macOS)<br>`%APPDATA%\\\\Claude\\\\claude_desktop_config.json` (Windows) | [Claude Desktop MCP Setup](https://support.claude.com/en/articles/10949351-getting-started-with-local-mcp-servers-on-claude-desktop) |\\n294:[GitHub Copilot CLI](https://github.blog/changelog/2026-01-14-github-copilot-cli-enhanced-agents-context-management-and-new-ways-to-install/) supports MCP servers via the `/mcp` command.\\n299:#### Add Azure MCP Server\\n301:1. In a Copilot CLI session, run `/mcp add` to open the MCP server configuration form.\\n309:   | **Command** | `npx -y @azure/mcp@latest server start` |\\n319:Verify the MCP server is configured by running:\\n328:● MCP Server Configuration:\\n329:  • azure-mcp (local): Command: npx\\n335:#### Managing MCP Servers\\n345:The [GitHub Copilot SDK](https://github.com/github/copilot-sdk) enables programmatic integration of Azure MCP tools into your applications across multiple languages.\\n350:# Using GitHub Copilot SDK with Azure MCP\\n<!--\\nSee eng\\\\scripts\\\\Process-PackageReadMe.ps1 for instruction on how to annotate this README.md for package specific output\\n-->\\n# <!-- remove-section: start nuget;vsix remove_azure_logo --><img height=\\\"36\\\" width=\\\"36\\\" src=\\\"https://cdn-dynmedia-1.microsoft.com/is/content/microsoftcorp/acom_social_icon_azure\\\" alt=\\\"Microsoft Azure Logo\\\" /> <!-- remove-section: end remove_azure_logo -->Azure MCP Server <!-- insert-section: nuget;vsix;npm;pypi {{ToolTitle}} -->\\n<!-- remove-section: start nuget;vsix;npm;pypi remove_note_ga -->\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> Azure MCP Server 2.0 is now [generally available](https://aka.ms/azmcp/2.0-ga).\\n<!-- remove-sectio"},"sessionId":"2026-09-23T03-58-32-231Z_01a0cc6a-4726-71f4-b47c-57674e2cf3d3","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:02:27.346Z","toolInput":"{\"code\":\"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\\\"rg -n 'MCP|mcpServers|npx|network|entra|app registration|app registration' /tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/README.md | head -60; sed -n '1,130p' /tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/README.md; rg -n 'app.*(create|list)|entra.*app|virtual network|vnet' /tmp/microsoft-mcp/servers/Azure.Mcp.Server/README.md | head -40\\\",workdir:\\\"/home/chris/01_Projects/azure/homelab\\\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:4500}); text(r.output)\\n\"}","toolName":"exec","toolOutput":"[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"jetbrains.com/plugin/8053) [![Install Azure MCP in Eclipse](https://img.shields.io/badge/Eclipse-Install_Azure_MCP_Server-b6ae1d?style=flat-square&logo=eclipse&logoColor=white)](htt