ce changes."},"sessionId":"2026-09-23T03-58-32-231Z_01a0cc6a-4726-71f4-b47c-57674e2cf3d3","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:02:44.669Z","toolInput":"install mcp servers needed for managing azure iaas, vnets, vms, admins, app registrations from https://github.com/microsoft/mcp into this project","toolName":"conversation","toolOutput":"Added **Microsoft Azure MCP** in [`.mcp.json`](/home/chris/01_Projects/azure/homelab/.mcp.json), using the official `@azure/mcp` server. It’s configured read-only by default; sign in to Azure separately so the server can authenticate.\n\nThe unified Azure server is intended to cover Azure infrastructure such as VMs and virtual networks. I haven’t verified that it exposes every requested admin or app-registration operation, or connected to an Azure account. Enable write access only when you’re ready to permit resource changes."},"type":"raw"}}␀␀␀�3␀���